  "modified": "2026-10-29T14:36:05Z",
  "details": "- Rebuild with golang 1.22.9-1.el9_2.tuxcare.els30 and patch vendored\n  golang.org/x/net/http2 to fix CVE-2026-78667, CVE-2026-78669\n- CVE-2026-78667: net/http: limit the number of ranges parsed from a Range\n  header in FileServer, ServeContent and ServeFile to 200, ignoring headers\n  with too many ranges, to avoid excessive CPU and memory consumption (Go\n  standard library, fixed by the golang rebuild)\n- CVE-2026-78669: keep HTTP/2 stream send windows relative to the peer's\n  initial window size, so a SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE change no longer\n  walks every open stream and a malicious peer can no longer exhaust CPU\n  with many small SETTINGS frames, in the golang.org/x/net/http2 copy\n  vendored by podman and in the Go standard library (golang rebuild)",
